= Knowledge request =

Structured operational record for [[BITwiki:Requested knowledge]]. It preserves the distinction between a missing-knowledge signal and a canonical knowledge object while giving the request lifecycle a real queryable substrate.

== Usage ==

<pre>
{{Knowledge request
 |request=Sequence alignment
 |reason=Foundational Bioinformatics coverage gap
 |candidate_domains=Biology,Computer science
 |source_leads=
 |needed_depth=full page
 |status=requested
 |canonical_page=
 |notes=
}}
</pre>

The template stores one row in Cargo table <code>Knowledge_requests</code> and renders that record as a row in the public request table.

== Contract ==

* <code>request</code>, <code>reason</code>, <code>needed_depth</code>, and <code>status</code> are required by repository workflow validation.
* <code>status</code> is one of: <code>requested</code>, <code>researching</code>, <code>drafting</code>, <code>review</code>, <code>satisfied</code>, <code>declined</code>.
* Candidate Domains, when supplied, must already exist in the controlled Domain vocabulary. A request is not permission to invent a Domain.
* Active requests must not already exist as canonical Main-namespace pages.
* <code>satisfied</code> requires <code>canonical_page</code> to point to source-controlled canonical content.
* Request titles are unique within the Cargo table and within the source-controlled queue.

== Cargo lifecycle ==

Saving this template does '''not''' create the database table. After deployment, an authorized operator must create or recreate <code>Knowledge_requests</code> from this template using Cargo's Create/Recreate data action or the Cargo maintenance command documented in [[BITwiki:Deployment prerequisites]].

Cargo is used here for repeated operational records. It does not replace Semantic MediaWiki for knowledge-graph assertions.

